<section class="p-hero"><div class="p-hero-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/sf-victorians.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/sf-victorians-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/sf-victorians.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="680" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap p-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/city-coverage/">City coverage</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">San Francisco</span></nav><p class="kicker">Bay Area</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in San Francisco, California</h1><p class="lede">Victorians, Edwardians, attached Sunset homes and condo towers: San Francisco claims are shaped by shared walls, steep lots and old buildings.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-copper" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/get-in-touch/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>City and County of San Francisco</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Bay Area</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks in San Francisco</b><ul class="chips"><li>Water between units</li><li>Earthquake &amp; fire following</li><li>Wind-driven rain</li><li>Fire in older buildings</li><li>Soft-story buildings</li></ul><p class="hoods"><b>Neighborhoods we often work in:</b> Sunset, Richmond, Marina, Noe Valley, Bernal Heights, Mission</p></div>

<h2>Old buildings, shared walls</h2>
<p>Much of San Francisco was built in the decades after 1906, and many Victorian and Edwardian buildings remain. Row houses in the Sunset and Richmond share walls, and many buildings have been converted to condominiums or tenancies-in-common. A fire or water loss in one unit regularly affects neighbors, and determining which policy pays for which damage is half the work of an insurance appraiser in San Francisco.</p>
<h2>Earthquake history and retrofits</h2>
<p>The 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake caused severe damage in the Marina District, where buildings on fill suffered liquefaction and fires broke out. The city later adopted a mandatory soft-story retrofit program for many older wood-frame buildings with ground-floor garages. Earthquake damage requires separate coverage, but fire following an earthquake is generally covered under standard policies.</p>
<h2>Wind-driven rain and water losses</h2>
<p>Atmospheric rivers, like the series that hit in winter 2022–23, push rain into older buildings through windows, parapets and siding. Water damage between units, from bathrooms, kitchens and failed supply lines, is the most common claim type in the city’s multi-unit buildings.</p>
<h2>Repair costs</h2>
<p>San Francisco has some of the highest construction costs in the country. Parking restrictions, permit timelines, historic preservation requirements and the need to match ornate millwork and plaster all add to repair costs. Estimates priced for suburban work often miss these factors, which is one of the most common reasons we find a significant gap.</p>
<h3>Condos and TICs</h3>
<p>For condos, we review the HOA master policy and CC&amp;Rs alongside the owner’s unit policy. For tenancies-in-common, we look at the building policy and the TIC agreement to see who is responsible for what.</p>

<h2>Services available in San Francisco</h2>
<p>Every California Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in San Francisco and the rest of City and County of San Francisco, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/policyholder-appraiser-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/home-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/commercial-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/roof-damage-appraisal/">Roof Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/santa-ana-wind-damage-appraisal/">Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/atmospheric-river-storm-claim-appraisal/">Atmospheric River &amp; Storm Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/water-leak-claim-appraisal/">Water Leak Claim Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from San Francisco property owners</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary>Who pays when water from my upstairs neighbor damages my unit?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Often the upstairs owner’s policy or the HOA master policy, depending on the source and the governing documents. Your own policy may also respond.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are San Francisco repair costs reflected in standard estimates?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Not always. Access, permits, historic finishes and local labor rates often need to be priced specifically.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does my policy cover earthquake damage?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Usually not without separate earthquake coverage. Fire following an earthquake is generally covered.</p></div></details></div>
